O<probe_corner> sub
(Call: O<probe_corner> call [X Dir 1/-1] [Y Dir 1/-1] [Probe Dia] [Search Dist] [Fast Feed] [Edge Overlap])

#<x_dir> = #1
#<y_dir> = #2
#<probe_dia> = #3
#<search_dist> = #4
#<fast_feed> = #5
#<overlap> = #6

(1. X PROBE)
O<probe_edge> call [1] [#<x_dir>] [#<probe_dia>] [#<search_dist>] [#<fast_feed>]

(Probe edge finishes in G90 mode. X WCS is now 0. Probe is resting exactly 2mm away)

(2. Switch to Incremental mode for corner navigation)
G91

(3. Y CORNER DISTANCE - Move Y backward to clear the corner)
#<y_move> = [#<overlap> * -#<y_dir>]
G0 Y#<y_move>

(4. X CORNER DISTANCE - Move X over the part to prepare for Y probe)
(Since we are 2mm away from the edge, we add 2.0 to the overlap to get fully across)
#<x_move> = [[#<overlap> * #<x_dir>] + [2.0 * #<x_dir>]]
G0 X#<x_move>

(5. Switch back to Absolute mode before calling the next probe)
G90

(6. Y PROBE)
O<probe_edge> call [2] [#<y_dir>] [#<probe_dia>] [#<search_dist>] [#<fast_feed>]

(7. OPTIONAL BACKOFF - Return Y to the corner start position)
G91
G0 Y[#<overlap> * -#<y_dir>]
G90

O<probe_corner> endsub
M2